<DocsLayout
  title="Compatibility overview: what 83/83 means"
  description="The niubash engine passes 83/83 of GNU Bash 5.3's upstream test corpora, byte-identical output on 82 suites; true-baseline differential method, byte-identical semantics, extra corpora, and the 'compatible ≠ same implementation' stance."
  path="/en/docs/compatibility/"
  lang="en"
  enPath="/docs/compatibility/"
  zhBanner
  jsonLdExtra={faqJsonLd(pageFaq, 'en')}
>
  <header class="doc-head">
    <h1>Compatibility overview: what 83/83 means</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      "Bash compatible" is a sentence anyone can say. niubash's version is
      <strong>measured, not claimed</strong>: take GNU Bash's own 83 upstream test corpora, run a
      true-baseline bidirectional differential on real Windows hardware, and the result is 83/83
      passing with 82 suites byte-identical in output — the single residual proven byte-for-byte to
      be a race inside GNU Bash itself. This page explains exactly what those numbers mean and how
      they were measured.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>What a true-baseline differential is</h2>
    <p>
      The easiest place to water down a compatibility measurement is the baseline. Run upstream tests
      without pinning the environment, or let script stubs stand in for real tools, and the pass rate
      means nothing. rubash's ledger (full rerun 2026-10-12 on master <code>764b9dde</code>) records
      the baseline discipline: no upstream test stubs, real <code>/bin/sh</code> mounted by niu, a
      per-suite <code>TMPDIR</code>, foreground timeout control; a pure-baseline failure set is run
      first on the same machine and environment, and <strong>the bidirectional comm must be empty
      before anything counts</strong> — directional differences in either direction (GNU fails / engine
      passes, or engine fails / GNU passes) must be driven to zero. Environment-bound differences
      (NTFS attribute bits, locale, host tool output, <code>/dev/tty</code>…) are audited item by item
      before counting as zero.
    </p>
    <details class="zh-fold">
      <summary>中文原文 · Chinese original</summary>
      <div lang="zh-CN">
        <p>
          兼容性测量最容易掺水的环节是「基线」。跑上游测试却不固定环境、或让脚本桩替代
          真实工具，测出的通过率毫无意义。rubash 的台账（2026-10-12 在 master
          <code>764b9dde</code> 全量复跑）记录了基线纪律：不使用上游脚本桩、由 niu
          挂载真实的 <code>/bin/sh</code>、每套件独立 <code>TMPDIR</code>、前台超时控制；
          同机同环境先跑纯基线失败集，<strong>双向 comm 为空才放行</strong>——即 GNU
          失败而引擎通过、或引擎失败而 GNU 通过的方向性差异都要归零。环境绑定差异
          （NTFS 属性位、locale、宿主工具输出、<code>/dev/tty</code> 等）逐项审计后才计为零。
        </p>
        <p>
          语义判定的一手依据是仓内 vendored 的 GNU bash-5.3 源码：每个行为主张给出
          <code>file:line</code> 坐标；WSL 里的 GNU 5.3.0 只做行为验证。GPL 代码零拷贝，
          判定纪律成文于 PROVENANCE 文档。
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What 83/83 and 82 byte-identical suites mean</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Metric</th><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>PASS</td>
          <td><strong>83/83 (100%)</strong></td>
          <td>All 83 suites of GNU Bash 5.3's upstream test corpora pass, nameref included.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Byte-identical</td>
          <td><strong>82 suites (0 diff)</strong></td>
          <td>Output byte-for-byte identical to GNU — not "semantically equivalent": an empty byte-level diff.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>nameref residual</td>
          <td>1 line</td>
          <td>A visibility difference for <code>declare -r RO_PID</code> after coproc, proven to be GNU 5.3.0's own coproc reaping race (below).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Environmental deltas</td>
          <td>9 suites zeroed</td>
          <td>Difference items in the glob/extglob/read/coproc suites are all environment-bound (NTFS, locale, signal tables…); audited to zero after A/B double-commit agreement per suite.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <details class="zh-fold">
      <summary>中文原文 · Chinese original</summary>
      <div lang="zh-CN">
        <p>
          那一行 nameref 残差值得单独讲：在同一套 harness 文件系统上，<strong>GNU Bash
          对自己</strong>就能在 59/60 与 1/60 之间翻转这一行的输出；而在 ext4 上 GNU
          60/60 稳定，其输出与 rubash 逐字节一致（stdout 与 stderr 皆是）。结论：
          残差属于 GNU 自身的 reap 时序竞态，不是引擎缺陷——归因论证以逐字节证据成文。
          作为参照，2026-09-09 原始差分尚有 3427 处，此后削减 99% 以上：83/83
          是长跑的终点，不是起点的宣言。
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Corpora beyond the GNU suites</h2>
    <p>
      The same true-baseline method (script files, byte-level diff against GNU 5.3.0) is also applied
      to evaluation corpora outside the GNU suites and to real-world ecosystem assets; every judgment
      and count is archived in rubash issue #477:
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Corpus</th><th>Result</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>modernish capability suite (cross-shell quirk probes)</td><td><strong>166/166 identical rc vectors</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>mvdan/sh parser corpus</td><td>559 snippets; parse acceptance and exit codes aligned</td></tr>
        <tr><td>bash-completion matrix</td><td>452/452; <code>bash -n</code> canary byte-identical</td></tr>
        <tr><td>git-completion</td><td>140/140</td></tr>
        <tr><td>oh-my-bash</td><td>22 library loads, 252/252 function environments identical, 5 theme PS1s byte-identical</td></tr>
        <tr><td>ble.sh (29,601-line line-editing framework)</td><td><code>bash -n</code> rc=0 aligned; source mode terminates cleanly</td></tr>
        <tr><td>nvm.sh v0.40.x loader</td><td>Loads byte-clean (including empty <code>NVM_DIR</code> auto-use on native Windows)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>FFmpeg / OpenSSH / PHP / ltmain / cmake configure</td><td><code>--help</code> and error-path output byte-identical</td></tr>
        <tr><td>git's own test framework t/test-lib.sh</td><td>Runs end-to-end under the engine</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <details class="zh-fold">
      <summary>中文原文 · Chinese original</summary>
      <div lang="zh-CN">
        <p>
          上述资产全部钉为回归夹具在 CI 每次推送时运行；真实生态收割语料（数千仓、近万
          资产，夜间巡检）持续把发现的真实缺陷回流为修复。
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Compatible ≠ same implementation</h2>
    <p>
      These numbers prove consistency of the <strong>script-observable surface</strong>: exit codes,
      stdout/stderr bytes, fd behavior, signal disposition. They do not say the internals match bash —
      quite the opposite: subshells and command substitution create zero processes (see the
      <a href="/en/docs/execution-model/">execution model</a>), path translation is table-driven with
      no MSYS layer (see <a href="/en/docs/paths-and-msys/">paths &amp; MSYS</a>). Differences are
      framed by contract documents and the ledger is public (environment-zeroed items are named per
      suite) — the other half of "compatibility is measured": prove where things agree, and write
      down where they do not.
    </p>
  </section>

  <footer class="further">
    <h2>Read further</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://unixwin.github.io/niubash/rubash-bash-compat-matrix/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bash compatibility matrix (official niubash docs) ↗</a></li>
